# ---- Generated outputs ----
# outputs/ is regenerable via scripts and notebooks. The small results
# summaries under outputs/results/ are force-added (see .gitignore exception)
# so the README links resolve, but heavy artefacts (model checkpoints, figure
# dumps, sweep intermediates) are not committed.
outputs/*
!outputs/results/
outputs/results/*
!outputs/results/results.json
!outputs/results/results_summary.md
# The paper's figures, on the same reasoning as the results summaries: a draft
# whose figures are not in the tree is a draft whose figures do not resolve.
# PNG for reading, PDF for typesetting, and the manifest that records which
# artefact digests each was drawn from. Regenerable by
# `python scripts/make_figures_g15.py`.
!outputs/figures_g15/
outputs/figures_g15/*
!outputs/figures_g15/*.png
!outputs/figures_g15/*.pdf
!outputs/figures_g15/manifest.json
# Cited by papers/draft.md section 4.3. Regenerable by
# `python scripts/floor_sensitivity_g15.py`; reads committed artefacts only.
!outputs/floor_sensitivity_g15/
outputs/floor_sensitivity_g15/*
!outputs/floor_sensitivity_g15/floor_sensitivity.json
!outputs/floor_sensitivity_g15/manifest.json
# The Windows-leg scoring evidence of docs/WINDOWS_LEG_SCORED_g15.md.
!outputs/ci_local_g15/
!outputs/nb02_ordering_g15/

# Trained model checkpoints (regenerable)
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# Colab / Drive mounts
/content/
